[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes the C branches on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **A. Runtime options / modes.** The only runtime-selectable mode in the whole
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m library is the pair of `C2_TYPE` tags handed to `collided` (`lib.h:1-4`). They
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m drive a nested `switch` (`lib.c:74-97`) with 4 valid combinations, and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `AABB × CIRCLE` arm *swaps* the operands (`c2CircletoAABB(*(c2Circle*)B, *(c2AABB*)A)`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m — B is the circle, A is the box). There are no `#ifdef`s, no global state, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m init/config struct, and no flags.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **B. Entry points — all 10 exported symbols, lowest level first.** Phase B drives
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the low-level ones (`c2V`, `c2Maxv`, `c2Minv`, `c2Clampv`, `c2Sub`, `c2Dot`)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m directly, not only through the `collided` one-shot wrapper, and also drives the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m mid-level predicates (`c2CircletoCircle`, `c2CircletoAABB`, `c2AABBtoAABB`)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m directly as well as through `collided`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **C. Input shapes.** Every parameter is a `float` (or a struct of floats), and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m C validates nothing, so **all 2^32 bit patterns are valid input**. The classes the
